 "The batch record is the birth certificate of a medicine lot: the complete, contemporaneous record of everything done to make it - materials weighed with lot numbers, equipment used, process parameters, in-process test results, yields, deviations, and the signatures of everyone who performed or checked each step. Master formulas define what should happen; executed batch records prove what did happen. Reviewers check every entry before release: a missing signature or unexplained gap stops the batch. The industry's founding rule applies: if it isn't written down, it didn't happen - and if it didn't happen as written, the batch is suspect.",
