 "Identity, Strength, Quality, Purity: The Four Demands",
 "Every medicine must meet four demands, and manufacturing quality exists to guarantee all four, every batch. Identity: the product is what the label claims - no mix-ups, no mislabeling. Strength: each unit contains the labeled amount of active ingredient, within tight limits. Quality: it meets all specifications - dissolution, uniformity, appearance. Purity: it is free from contamination and excessive impurities or degradation products. Fail any one and the batch cannot be released, however expensive it was to make. These four words are the acceptance criteria for the entire manufacturing enterprise.",
